# This repository had no .gitignore at all until 2026-10-07.
#
# The two-repo split (Jira GRW-369 · GRW-370) moved `web/` out of the monorepo
# and left the rules behind: the API repo still carries `web/.next/`,
# `web/next-env.d.ts`, `web/AGENTS.md` and `web/CLAUDE.md` in ITS ignore file,
# where they now match nothing. Here they matched nothing either, because the
# file did not exist — so `node_modules` (391M), `.next` (1.3G) and the
# generated files below all sat in `git status` as untracked, one `git add -A`
# away from the history. Nothing junk had been committed; every file was
# staged by name instead, which is not a thing to rely on twice.

# No trailing slash, copied deliberately from the API repo's own comment:
# `node_modules/` matches only a directory, which is how a worktree's
# node_modules SYMLINK got committed there (4f00168) and replaced the real
# folder on merge.
node_modules

# Next's build output and the types it writes on `dev`/`build`.
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Next installs these agent rules into the repo root ("BEGIN:nextjs-agent-rules");
# CLAUDE.md is one line importing AGENTS.md. Generated, not authored — the API
# repo made the same call for them when they lived at `web/`.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md

# Secrets never committed (conventions, 06 §6): real values belong in SSM.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.test
.env.production

# A salon's own catalogue, converted for onboarding (menu PDF, services and
# packages). Real business data and a one-off working set, not product code —
# kept on disk, out of the history. Track a particular import deliberately if
# it ever needs sharing.
imports/

.claude/settings.local.json
coverage/
*.log
.DS_Store
